/* ================================================================
   SITE CONTENT - TEXTS: SHORT LABELS & DICTIONARIES (French / English)
   ================================================================
   This file holds ONLY text data - no behaviour, no layout.
   It is loaded by index.html before every other script, so the
   dictionaries below are available to the whole site.

   WHAT IS HERE
     SHARED  Labels shared by every page: site navigation, header,
             footer, search and viewer buttons. Used by
             assets/app.js.
     PAGE    One entry per page section, keyed by the data-i18n
             attributes in index.html: headings, leads, card
             titles, metrics, form labels...

   HOW TO EDIT
     - Every string exists twice: "fr" first, then "en".
       Always change BOTH languages, in the same place.
     - Keep the key names unchanged: index.html and app.js look
       strings up by key; a renamed key silently stops working.
     - New label needed? Add the key here (both languages), then
       put data-i18n="yourKey" on the element in index.html.
     - Longer passages are NOT here either: each page keeps its
       own long texts in assets/content-page-<page>.js (one entry
       per passage: key, French, English) - edit them there.

   The other content files (all under assets/, all data-only):
     content-page-<page>.js   long texts, one file per page:
                              global, home, bio, library, courses,
                              media, events, egov-days, partners,
                              documents, contact
     content-library.js       the publication catalogue (LIB)
     content-certificates.js  the certificate / document viewer
                              registry (CERTVIEW): pages, summaries,
                              gallery captions
     content-scholar.js       the Google Scholar metrics (SCHOLAR)
     subtitles.js             generated subtitle data (do not edit)
   ================================================================ */

